# PDV
(Phaethon Dynasty Imperial Vanguard)

The Vanguard is an isolated imperialistic monarchy located in the Colossus sector and possibly adjacent bodies of space that are currently deemed undiscovered. Initially a group of feudal bodies lost to the history books, now a large Sultanate regime wielding old syndicate technologies scavenged after the Corporate Wars' conclusion. Known as the native inhabitants of the Perseus Arm, they are hell bent on evicting the encroaching Trans-Solarian-Federation and obtaining complete control over the independent industries of Colossus.

   Fueled by an ever-growing industry and their reverse-engineered equipment littering their territory, the [D4BC7B=olive]PDV[/color] wield their ballistic weaponry with a heavy and unforgiving hand.
   While smaller in number compared to the broader [color=cyan]TSFMC[/color], the Dynasty is nowhere near weak in comparison to their foes detache that are nearly entirely stranded at their doorstep, it is a boon that their sectors [color=pink]anomalous activities[/color] prevents their enemies from gaining the upper hand.
   They are capable of using their mobility and brutal tactics to separate their enemies in number and eliminate them one by one until they are victorious. No cost too great, every death repaid with interest, that is the way their Sultans' Grand Vizier(s) operate.

   The Phaethon Dynasty Vanguard has been given a simple directive by their commanding Sultanate:

  > Destabilize the region to prepare it for Dynasty occupation.

   The Grand Vizier and their closest associates, the Asvarans, ensure that the Vanguard acts in the Sultanates best interests. Securing Phaethon smuggling operations and routing them to the correct locations. Preventing the TSFMC from doing the same. Acquiring assets for various purposes from the sectors independents and the enemy.

   A [color=purple]Grand Vizier[/color] is the highest ranking within the Dynasty and closest to the Sultanate of the Vanguard. They have the final say in any matter regarding operations. Denying the request of a Vizier is no different from high treason to the Dynasty. While the Vanguard is capable of acting without a leader to direct their fury there is nothing more terrifying than a leader who can rally their soldiers.
   It does not matter how the Vanguard is victorious, only that it is, ensure your Sultans' wishes are reality and that your honor is upheld through even your newest of bloods.

   As the [color=gold]Asvaran[/color] it is your duty to follow the Grand Vizier and delegate the Vanguard as they see fit. In the event there is no Vizier you are the one who must take up their mantle even if it is only for a time.

   [color=silver]Denasvar[/color], while not much more than your average foot soldier, is considered a more experienced and leadership capable position. They are generally picked above others for leading smaller detachments of Rahkshan. Be the guiding force among your peers.

   [color=bronze]Rahkshan[/color] are arguably the backbone of the Vanguard. Necessary for success because without a foot soldier you have no army. You are the rage of the Sultan. Act with purpose and follow the will of your [color=purple]Grand Vizier[/color]. Dying in the heat of combat is your highest honor. Living to reap the benefits of your Sultans' many victories, large and small, is a privilege.

   [color=red]Spasaka[/color]. You shouldn't encounter Spasaka in any event, at least not without them allowing it, sometimes Spasaka disguise themselves even to their own peers to ensure their identity is ambiguous. Specialists designed around infiltration and espionage. They are equipped with old Syndicate agent technology capable of altering many aspects of their persona. One thing that a Spasaka must always do, however, is ensure that their goals are in line with their commanders'. Keeping close contact with the Vanguard during their work is key to proper information gathering and window opening.

  [color=gray]Cyborgs[/color] are reverse-engineered automatons capable of assisting in various fields. Constructed by the finest minds of the Dynasty and ready to serve any orders given to them by the Vanguard.

